    "conventions": "Family name first, then a given name of one or two syllables: Wang Fang, Li Haoran. A few hundred family names cover almost everyone, and the most common (Wang, Li, Zhang, Liu, Chen) are shared by tens of millions. Northern and southern cities differ in which family names are most common: Chen, Huang, Liang and Lin are everywhere in Guangdong, Shen, Gu, Qian and Xu around Shanghai and Hangzhou. Names are written here in Pinyin without tone marks, as on passports. Friends add Xiao (young) or Lao (old) before a family name (Xiao Wang, Lao Zhang); many office workers, especially in tech and foreign firms, also use an English name such as Kevin or Coco.",
